<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18991" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fullōnĭcus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		fullo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to fullers.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pila,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 10, 5</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">14, 2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Subst.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fullōnĭca</span></b> , ae,
				f.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> (Sc. ars.) <i>The fuller's craft</i>, <i>fulling</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si non didicisti fullonicam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. As. 5, 2, 57</span></i>
			 (dub. fulloniam, Fleck.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fullonicam docere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. 1, 18, 21</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vitr. 6 praef.</span></i> §
			7.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> (Sc.
			officina.) <i>A fuller's shop</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eum, in cujus fundo aqua oritur, fullonicas
					circa fontem instituisse,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					39, 3, 3</span></i>
			; also, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fullonica</span></b> ,
				orum, n., <i><span class="en">ib. 7, 1, 13, § 8</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
